 Knowledge & Learning
Quiz / Test Scores – Performance in Python/SQL/Big Data/other topic quizzes.
Concept Understanding – Ability to explain concepts clearly in discussions.
Problem-Solving – Accuracy and efficiency in solving coding/analytical problems.
 Engagement & Participation
Active Participation – Asking questions, contributing to group discussions.
Collaboration – Helping peers, sharing knowledge in group activities.
Consistency – Regular attendance, timely completion of exercises.
  Practical Application
Project Work / Mini Assignments – Quality, creativity, and correctness of project submissions.
Real-world Thinking – How well they apply concepts to solve realistic scenarios.
Code Quality – Clean, efficient, and well-documented coding style.
 Soft Skills & Attitude
Curiosity – Showing initiative to explore beyond the syllabus.
Communication Skills – Explaining solutions clearly in presentations or demos.
Adaptability – Quick learning and ability to fix mistakes.
Team Spirit – Collaboration and positive contribution to team activities.
 Fun / Extra Recognition (optional)
Most Improved Trainee – Growth from start to end of training.
Fastest Debugger / Problem Solver – Quick turnaround in exercises.
Best Innovator – Unique/creative solution in a project.
Consistency Champion – Never missed deadlines or tasks.
  Best Practice:
Objective + subjective criteria (e.g., quiz scores + team spirit).
If possible, have multiple small prizes 
Best Coder, 
Best Team Player, 
Most Improved


